  "notes": "The purest loop-forward entry in this batch: **\"one recognisable sample carried nearly intact\"** — a single looped figure with minimal added instrumentation, \"one of the clearest 'loop-forward' approaches in this lane\", with added parts limited to \"a pad or a filtered doubling\". Three parameters follow from that sentence and nothing else does. (1) The drums are subordinate: `hihat.velocities.main` tops at 0.75, `snare.offGridMs` 8 for the laid-back placement, `quantizeStrength` 0.72, and the kit never takes an accent off the loop. (2) The harmony is *inherited*, not written — his method is single-source flipping, so the scale set is major-mode (`major`/`mixolydian` ahead of the minors), the families are the g-funk hybrid of a major-mode source over minor-inflected bass, and `chordToneBias` is 0.80 because the melody is the source record playing itself back. (3) The countermelody is the pad: `sustain_pad` sits between `octave_echo` (the \"filtered doubling\") and `answer_lick`, at `densityRatio` 0.30 — the floor, because the research says added parts are *limited*. The 808 is \"a sustained sub reinforcing the sample's root motion, E1–C2, no trap glides\": `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.90 with `glideProb` 0.05, not a slide part. ⚠ `medium`, and the research names the hole: \"credits, lineage and loop-forward method documented; drum programming detail partly inferred **[LOW-CONF]**\". Every drum number below is that inference. ⚠ `switchUpProb` 0.02 is deliberate — the research says \"no beat switch\", and the breakdown that exposes the sample is modeled as the bridge instead. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.6 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.6 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub.",
